1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:15,000
<font color="#FF8040">{\an8}Downloaded From MoviesMod.Org</font>

2
00:00:06,006 --> 00:00:08,008
♪ Tell me I'm a setback ♪

3
00:00:09,009 --> 00:00:11,636
♪ Tell me that I'm bad for you ♪

4
00:00:11,720 --> 00:00:13,722
♪ Say we had a good game ♪

5
00:00:14,806 --> 00:00:17,267
♪ But someone had to lose ♪

6
00:00:17,350 --> 00:00:19,352
♪ I think we took a wrong turn ♪

7
00:00:20,395 --> 00:00:23,148
♪ Somewhere along the way ♪

8
00:00:23,231 --> 00:00:25,442
♪ So now I'll take a step back ♪

9
00:00:26,609 --> 00:00:29,070
♪ So you can have your space ♪

10
00:00:30,822 --> 00:00:33,658
♪ You said you loved me regardless ♪

11
00:00:33,742 --> 00:00:35,994
♪ Now look at the problems you started ♪

12
00:00:36,536 --> 00:00:39,164
♪ In love with a struggling artist ♪

13
00:00:39,247 --> 00:00:41,583
♪ I wasn't what you really wanted… ♪

14
00:00:41,666 --> 00:00:43,293
Ready, go, hut!

15
00:00:43,376 --> 00:00:45,962
♪ Pastime that you can't let go of ♪

16
00:00:47,005 --> 00:00:47,881
♪ Go of ♪

17
00:00:48,381 --> 00:00:50,800
-♪ Well, maybe I'm a landmine… ♪
-[whistle blows]

18
00:00:50,884 --> 00:00:53,261
Newsome! What the hell happened?

19
00:00:53,344 --> 00:00:55,096
Sorry, Coach, I misread the coverage.

20
00:00:55,180 --> 00:00:58,600
We're 0-4. Maybe act like
you've seen a football before.

21
00:01:03,354 --> 00:01:04,856
Hey, Coach, should I start warming up?

22
00:01:05,440 --> 00:01:06,441
-No.
-No.

23
00:01:08,151 --> 00:01:10,945
Oh, look, hey, I got a call
with the superintendent in five minutes,

24
00:01:11,029 --> 00:01:16,326
so just keep having them do long passes
until our QB successfully completes one!

25
00:01:16,409 --> 00:01:17,994
-[boy] You be running sprints!
-Copy that.

26
00:01:18,578 --> 00:01:19,579
Glad to have you.

27
00:01:19,662 --> 00:01:21,664
[indistinct chatter]

28
00:01:24,250 --> 00:01:27,128
All right, look alive, gentlemen.
Here comes Coach Walter.

29
00:01:27,837 --> 00:01:31,174
So, you and Allen finally ready
to let me run the ball, or…

30
00:01:31,257 --> 00:01:33,927
No. Zebra 34!

31
00:01:34,010 --> 00:01:35,929
[Dylan] Another passing play?
Come on, man.

32
00:01:36,012 --> 00:01:37,889
Not trying to wear out my arm
during a bye week.

33
00:01:37,972 --> 00:01:41,309
Looks like you're not trying at all
from where we're standing.

34
00:01:41,392 --> 00:01:44,270
Come on. You've been consistently
off target, missing receivers.

35
00:01:44,354 --> 00:01:46,523
You threw three picks last week.
You don't seem to care.

36
00:01:46,606 --> 00:01:49,776
You know, you're worse than my dad,
riding me like this. I care.

37
00:01:50,777 --> 00:01:51,778
Then prove it.

38
00:01:52,362 --> 00:01:53,696
Work on your passing.

39
00:01:55,156 --> 00:01:56,449
Zebra 34!

40
00:01:57,450 --> 00:01:58,284
[whistle blows]

41
00:01:58,368 --> 00:02:01,663
All right, boys, let's go.
You heard Coach. Ready!

42
00:02:02,539 --> 00:02:04,332
-[boys] Zebra 34.
-[boy] Zebra 34.

43
00:02:04,415 --> 00:02:05,500
[boy 2] All right, boys.

44
00:02:05,583 --> 00:02:08,461
-[chuckles] Watch this.
-[boy] Watch Mike! Watch Mike!

45
00:02:09,045 --> 00:02:09,879
Ready!

46
00:02:09,963 --> 00:02:11,339
[boy 2] Hey, fix that jersey.

47
00:02:11,422 --> 00:02:13,758
-Down, set, hut!
-[boy] Here we go.

48
00:02:14,259 --> 00:02:16,261
[rock music playing]

49
00:02:16,845 --> 00:02:18,054
[indistinct yelling]

50
00:02:18,138 --> 00:02:19,013
[boy] Goddamn!

51
00:02:19,681 --> 00:02:20,723
[boy 2] I'm on him! On him!

52
00:02:20,807 --> 00:02:22,267
[Dylan] Whoo-hoo-hoo-hoo!

53
00:02:22,350 --> 00:02:23,434
Let's go, baby.

54
00:02:25,603 --> 00:02:27,188
-[whistle blows]
-[boy] Come on.

55
00:02:27,689 --> 00:02:29,482
Hey, just gotta let me do me, Coach!

56
00:02:29,566 --> 00:02:30,775
Whoo!

57
00:02:30,859 --> 00:02:31,693
-Hey!
-[boy] Come on!

58
00:02:31,776 --> 00:02:32,902
[boy 2] Not even 34.

59
00:02:35,738 --> 00:02:37,824
You realize we could save time

60
00:02:37,907 --> 00:02:40,702
and avoid carpal tunnel
by whipping these up in Photoshop?

61
00:02:40,785 --> 00:02:43,997
Yes, but there's just something
about doing it by hand.

62
00:02:44,706 --> 00:02:48,168
Reminds me of this little thrift shop
in Greenpoint Lucy loved.

63
00:02:48,251 --> 00:02:50,545
I can always get down
with an arts and crafts sesh.

64
00:02:50,628 --> 00:02:51,671
Thanks, Danny.

65
00:02:53,464 --> 00:02:54,966
[phone dings]

66
00:03:01,222 --> 00:03:03,349
How did Cole take the news
about you and Erin?

67
00:03:03,933 --> 00:03:05,643
I haven't had the opportunity to tell him.

68
00:03:06,352 --> 00:03:07,854
You guys share a room.

69
00:03:07,937 --> 00:03:09,355
[Danny] What am I supposed to say?

70
00:03:09,439 --> 00:03:10,857
"Good night, sleep tight."

71
00:03:10,940 --> 00:03:13,359
"Oh, hope you don't mind
I'm dating your ex."

72
00:03:13,443 --> 00:03:16,070
The longer you drag this out,
the more likely he finds out

73
00:03:16,154 --> 00:03:18,156
in some other less ideal way.

74
00:03:19,824 --> 00:03:21,159
I'm gonna do it.

75
00:03:21,242 --> 00:03:22,285
Tonight.

76
00:03:22,368 --> 00:03:23,786
Good. You got this.

77
00:03:23,870 --> 00:03:25,413
[phone ringing]

78
00:03:26,539 --> 00:03:28,791
Go ahead. Tell Erin I said hi.

79
00:03:34,631 --> 00:03:36,799
Oh, nope, no. [chuckles]

80
00:03:36,883 --> 00:03:39,260
No taking out Gregory Peck
until you finish your homework.

81
00:03:39,344 --> 00:03:40,803
Maybe he could help?

82
00:03:40,887 --> 00:03:43,097
Oh, nice try, but I wasn't born yesterday.

83
00:03:43,181 --> 00:03:44,515
-Hey, Mom?
-Yeah?

84
00:03:44,599 --> 00:03:46,517
I need to take cookies
to the game this weekend.

85
00:03:46,601 --> 00:03:49,562
-Ooh. Do you wanna bake 'em with me later?
-Yeah.

86
00:03:49,646 --> 00:03:52,398
-Chocolate chip or oatmeal?
-Both.

87
00:03:52,899 --> 00:03:54,776
Hey, Jordan, how was your day?

88
00:03:54,859 --> 00:03:56,319
Better before this conversation.

89
00:03:58,780 --> 00:04:00,448
-[Katherine] Hi.
-Hi.

90
00:04:01,074 --> 00:04:03,284
Are you all ready for the pop-up tomorrow?

91
00:04:03,368 --> 00:04:04,535
Almost,

92
00:04:04,619 --> 00:04:07,455
but honestly, I'm still holding out
for a few more donations.

93
00:04:07,538 --> 00:04:10,041
We had to toss a box because someone
thought it was a trash can.

94
00:04:10,124 --> 00:04:13,169
-It was so gross.
-How much are you trying to raise again?

95
00:04:13,253 --> 00:04:14,379
A thousand dollars.

96
00:04:14,462 --> 00:04:17,048
You're welcome to dig through
my old stuff in your closet.

97
00:04:17,131 --> 00:04:18,132
Really?

98
00:04:18,216 --> 00:04:19,968
Of course. Take whatever you want.

99
00:04:20,051 --> 00:04:23,054
Just don't judge me
for my past fashion crimes.

100
00:04:24,389 --> 00:04:26,307
Exactly how bad are we talking here?

101
00:04:26,808 --> 00:04:28,726
Have you heard of the band Wham!?

102
00:04:29,519 --> 00:04:30,561
[Jackie chuckles]

103
00:04:38,820 --> 00:04:40,488
[country music playing on radio]

104
00:04:41,322 --> 00:04:42,907
I'm telling you, Gracie,

105
00:04:42,991 --> 00:04:46,077
this whole guest ranch business
is making me nervous.

106
00:04:46,160 --> 00:04:47,787
I mean, it's a bunch of yurts, Mom.

107
00:04:47,870 --> 00:04:49,914
It's a bunch of yurts for now.

108
00:04:50,415 --> 00:04:51,749
But before long,

109
00:04:51,833 --> 00:04:55,545
we're gonna be the next Telluride or Aspen

110
00:04:55,628 --> 00:04:59,340
with hotels and chains
and celebrity vacation homes.

111
00:04:59,424 --> 00:05:01,259
I mean, does that sound appealing to you?

112
00:05:01,342 --> 00:05:03,136
Maybe if it's the right celebrity.

113
00:05:03,219 --> 00:05:05,972
I mean, if Timothée Chalamet
wants to vacation here,

114
00:05:06,055 --> 00:05:08,099
I'll personally roll out the red carpet.

115
00:05:08,182 --> 00:05:10,435
Oh, it's all fun and games, honey.

116
00:05:11,019 --> 00:05:13,521
Until we can't afford
to live here anymore.

117
00:05:25,325 --> 00:05:26,617
[Alex] So have I gotten better?

118
00:05:26,701 --> 00:05:28,536
[indistinct chatter]

119
00:05:29,579 --> 00:05:30,997
-[Katherine] Hi, Grace.
-[Grace] Hey.

120
00:05:31,080 --> 00:05:33,041
-Jackie's upstairs.
-[Grace] Okay, thank you.

121
00:05:34,959 --> 00:05:36,294
-Hi.
-[Joanne] Hi.

122
00:05:37,295 --> 00:05:39,756
Thank you for having her over for dinner.

123
00:05:39,839 --> 00:05:42,216
Bob's working late,
and I have a… [clears throat]

124
00:05:42,300 --> 00:05:43,426
I have a thing.

125
00:05:43,509 --> 00:05:46,637
-Oh, she's welcome anytime. You know that.
-Okay.

126
00:05:47,972 --> 00:05:49,307
So, how have you been?

127
00:05:50,141 --> 00:05:52,352
I have been… okay.

128
00:05:53,436 --> 00:05:55,480
Just catching up on work stuff.

129
00:05:57,648 --> 00:05:58,483
Mm.

130
00:05:59,984 --> 00:06:03,404
Look, I'm gonna put us out of our misery
before we start talking about the weather.

131
00:06:03,488 --> 00:06:04,489
[sighs]

132
00:06:06,783 --> 00:06:08,743
Jo, you were
the first person I met in Silver Falls

133
00:06:08,826 --> 00:06:10,119
whose last name wasn't Walter.

134
00:06:11,162 --> 00:06:13,873
And I'm gonna do everything in my power
to make sure that this business

135
00:06:13,956 --> 00:06:15,917
doesn't encroach on
anybody's peace of mind,

136
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:20,380
but… I would really hate
for it to come between us.

137
00:06:22,882 --> 00:06:23,758
Me too.

138
00:06:25,885 --> 00:06:27,011
So we won't let it.

139
00:06:27,720 --> 00:06:29,138
-Okay?
-[Katherine] Okay.

140
00:06:29,222 --> 00:06:31,474
-I'll see you at book club. Okay.
-Yep.

141
00:06:31,974 --> 00:06:34,018
I have a lot to say about chapter five.

142
00:06:34,102 --> 00:06:36,104
[laughs]

143
00:06:41,359 --> 00:06:42,652
-[engine starts]
-[sighs]

144
00:06:46,447 --> 00:06:51,160
All right, Murph. We break our record,
there might be some treats in your future.

145
00:06:51,244 --> 00:06:52,078
Huh?

146
00:06:52,578 --> 00:06:53,413
[Blake] Last ride.

147
00:06:53,496 --> 00:06:56,541
Plant your boots, tip your hat,
and let's kick dust.

148
00:06:56,624 --> 00:06:58,626
[upbeat music playing]

149
00:07:02,964 --> 00:07:04,674
-[Alex] There we go.
-[horse neighs softly]

150
00:07:09,887 --> 00:07:10,972
[Alex] Come on, Murph.

151
00:07:18,187 --> 00:07:19,021
[Blake] And…

152
00:07:21,023 --> 00:07:21,858
time.

153
00:07:31,117 --> 00:07:33,244
-Okay.
-I'm impressed.

154
00:07:33,327 --> 00:07:34,287
Yeah?

155
00:07:34,370 --> 00:07:37,165
Impressed you didn't fall off,
'cause you were looking a little unsteady.

156
00:07:37,248 --> 00:07:39,667
But if we shorten your stirrups
and work on your core, then,

157
00:07:40,209 --> 00:07:41,294
you'll get there.

158
00:07:41,377 --> 00:07:42,462
And our time?

159
00:07:44,005 --> 00:07:46,382
Shaved off two seconds.
It's a new personal best.

160
00:07:46,883 --> 00:07:48,968
Okay. Could've led with that.

161
00:07:49,051 --> 00:07:51,471
I could've,
but it's also my job to keep you humble.

162
00:07:51,554 --> 00:07:52,472
[Alex chuckles]

163
00:07:52,555 --> 00:07:53,973
-[Blake] Nice work, pal.
-Thanks.

164
00:07:54,599 --> 00:07:56,559
-Oh, I was talking to the horse.
-[horse whinnies]

165
00:07:56,642 --> 00:07:58,936
Oh, she was talking to you. Hear that?

166
00:08:04,233 --> 00:08:06,569
What's the tea on Annie Oakley over there?

167
00:08:07,069 --> 00:08:09,322
Her name's Blake. She's 18,

168
00:08:09,405 --> 00:08:13,534
and she's teaching him how to not die
doing dangerous rodeo stuff.

169
00:08:14,118 --> 00:08:16,287
Are we sure that's all she's teaching him?

170
00:08:16,370 --> 00:08:21,125
I don't know, and I don't care.
He wanted space, so he's getting it.

171
00:08:23,753 --> 00:08:26,756
Holy shoulder pads, Batman!

172
00:08:26,839 --> 00:08:27,798
Like, can I borrow that?

173
00:08:28,799 --> 00:08:30,301
Only if you promise to lose it.

174
00:08:46,359 --> 00:08:47,443
What are those?

175
00:08:49,403 --> 00:08:51,113
They're my mom's.

176
00:08:55,952 --> 00:08:57,286
They're her designs.

177
00:09:03,626 --> 00:09:05,628
[emotional music playing]

178
00:09:17,139 --> 00:09:17,974
[Dylan] Ten!

179
00:09:18,057 --> 00:09:20,226
[exhales] Hoo!

180
00:09:20,726 --> 00:09:22,019
All right, boys, don't forget.

181
00:09:22,103 --> 00:09:24,188
Kegger at my place tonight, all right?
Invite only.

182
00:09:24,689 --> 00:09:25,773
What about your dad?

183
00:09:26,274 --> 00:09:28,484
Oh, if it doesn't affect my QB rating
or our record,

184
00:09:28,568 --> 00:09:30,403
he doesn't give a damn what I do.

185
00:09:30,486 --> 00:09:33,197
Plus, he's in Denver
with his new flavor of the week anyways.

186
00:09:33,281 --> 00:09:35,783
Hey, boys,
could you give us space for a sec?

187
00:09:38,411 --> 00:09:39,328
[Dylan scoffs]

188
00:09:40,621 --> 00:09:41,622
Sup, coach?

189
00:09:42,498 --> 00:09:46,043
You know what's up.
You ignored my play call out there today.

190
00:09:46,127 --> 00:09:47,837
Relax, bro. I was just having some fun.

191
00:09:47,920 --> 00:09:51,424
Have fun on your own time, okay?
When Coach isn't out there, I'm in charge.

192
00:09:51,507 --> 00:09:54,677
Yeah, but, um,
you're not really in charge, are you?

193
00:09:55,344 --> 00:09:57,179
What's your problem, huh?

194
00:09:57,263 --> 00:09:59,640
I thought you were happy
to have me back on the team.

195
00:10:01,142 --> 00:10:04,145
That was before I knew
you'd end up being Allen's little bitch.

196
00:10:09,817 --> 00:10:12,903
So, you're telling me you didn't know
you had ten designer dresses

197
00:10:12,987 --> 00:10:14,697
just chilling in your closet?

198
00:10:15,197 --> 00:10:19,285
Honestly, I mean, the days
before moving here were such a blur.

199
00:10:19,368 --> 00:10:21,704
People coming and going, boxes everywhere.

200
00:10:21,787 --> 00:10:24,373
I guess they got loaded up
with my things by mistake.

201
00:10:24,874 --> 00:10:27,251
Well, maybe we could sell a few
at the pop-up.

202
00:10:27,335 --> 00:10:30,046
I mean, I'm sure they'd go faster
than Mrs. Sapp's banana pudding

203
00:10:30,129 --> 00:10:31,380
at a church potluck.

204
00:10:33,716 --> 00:10:35,718
[emotional music playing]

205
00:10:37,845 --> 00:10:38,929
Oh my gosh.

206
00:10:39,430 --> 00:10:41,849
Oh my… Don't listen to me.
Sorry. I didn't even think about--

207
00:10:41,932 --> 00:10:43,392
No, I mean, you're right.

208
00:10:44,435 --> 00:10:48,230
Even with these last-minute donations,
we're still light on merchandise.

209
00:10:48,314 --> 00:10:50,775
Selling the dresses makes sense.

210
00:10:50,858 --> 00:10:53,444
Yeah… Hey, never mind.

211
00:10:53,527 --> 00:10:57,490
[chuckles] It's okay.
If we have to sacrifice a photo booth

212
00:10:57,573 --> 00:11:00,868
and ask Andrew Neville
from AP Euro to DJ, then so be it.

213
00:11:01,410 --> 00:11:03,621
It'll be great. Okay?

214
00:11:18,177 --> 00:11:19,345
Ho! Ho! Ho! Ho!

215
00:11:19,428 --> 00:11:21,931
Ho! Ho! Ho! Ho!

216
00:11:24,141 --> 00:11:26,310
-What are you doing?
-What are you doing?

217
00:11:26,394 --> 00:11:29,438
-Mr. Walter okayed the demo.
-That would be me. I'm Mr. Walter.

218
00:11:30,356 --> 00:11:31,899
The one in charge.

219
00:11:32,483 --> 00:11:33,317
The…

220
00:11:36,737 --> 00:11:39,907
Okay, just… Do not touch this shed. Okay?

221
00:11:45,621 --> 00:11:48,124
There's nothing you can do
to expedite the process?

222
00:11:48,999 --> 00:11:51,544
[man] No, not unless you have friends
at municipal planning.

223
00:11:51,627 --> 00:11:52,586
No. No, I don't.

224
00:11:53,254 --> 00:11:56,465
[man] Hey, well, the good news is that
the construction permits were approved.

225
00:11:56,549 --> 00:11:57,842
As soon as that shed's firewood,

226
00:11:57,925 --> 00:12:00,720
Richard wants us to start digging trenches
for the new utility line.

227
00:12:00,803 --> 00:12:02,847
-All right.
-Hey, Derren, it's George.

228
00:12:02,930 --> 00:12:05,266
I need to talk to my kid
for a minute, all right?

229
00:12:05,349 --> 00:12:07,435
-[Derren] Yeah. Sure thing, George.
-Thank you.

230
00:12:07,518 --> 00:12:08,436
I'll call back.

231
00:12:08,519 --> 00:12:09,478
[phone beeps]

232
00:12:10,396 --> 00:12:11,230
What's up?

233
00:12:11,897 --> 00:12:14,483
I just stopped a bulldozer
from tearing down the shed.

234
00:12:15,609 --> 00:12:17,027
You know anything about that?

235
00:12:18,028 --> 00:12:20,322
Dad, it's old.
It's got a hole in the roof,

236
00:12:20,990 --> 00:12:22,533
and we need utilities for our guests.

237
00:12:22,616 --> 00:12:25,828
You do not make decisions about my ranch
without talking to me first.

238
00:12:26,954 --> 00:12:30,332
Look, I am really trying to support
your vision and not micromanage this,

239
00:12:30,416 --> 00:12:35,171
but your great-great-grandfather
built that shed, all right?

240
00:12:35,254 --> 00:12:37,047
And I have memories there, so…

241
00:12:37,631 --> 00:12:41,177
Look, can't we just trench around it
and put the utilities on the other side?

242
00:12:41,260 --> 00:12:42,178
No, I--

243
00:12:42,261 --> 00:12:45,848
Okay, then move it. Move the shed. Put it…
Put it out where the silo used to be.

244
00:12:45,931 --> 00:12:48,893
Moving it would be twice as expensive
as demolishing it, and--

245
00:12:48,976 --> 00:12:50,394
-[phone ringing]
-Hang on.

246
00:12:51,437 --> 00:12:52,271
I should take this.

247
00:12:54,023 --> 00:12:56,192
Hey, Marlee,
thanks for getting back to me.

248
00:12:56,859 --> 00:12:58,694
Yeah. Question for you.

249
00:12:58,778 --> 00:13:01,363
Is your brother Pat still
at Colorado Parks and Wildlife?

250
00:13:06,452 --> 00:13:07,536
[Dylan] Hey!

251
00:13:09,038 --> 00:13:09,872
Cool if I sit?

252
00:13:10,998 --> 00:13:12,208
It's a free country.

253
00:13:13,793 --> 00:13:14,668
[Dylan] All right.

254
00:13:18,881 --> 00:13:19,882
[sighs]

255
00:13:21,342 --> 00:13:22,843
Best view in town, am I right?

256
00:13:23,761 --> 00:13:25,513
I like it better when it's quiet.

257
00:13:28,390 --> 00:13:31,519
You know, sometimes I come up here
and just… imagine

258
00:13:31,602 --> 00:13:33,604
what's happening
in those houses down there.

259
00:13:35,231 --> 00:13:36,649
Like the one with the red roof?

260
00:13:36,732 --> 00:13:38,943
Yeah, they're probably
sleeping off a rager.

261
00:13:39,860 --> 00:13:40,778
[chuckles]

262
00:13:41,320 --> 00:13:42,196
Or over there?

263
00:13:43,864 --> 00:13:47,701
You know, I bet you a second-grader is
defending his property from two burglars

264
00:13:47,785 --> 00:13:50,162
after his family left on vacation.

265
00:13:51,413 --> 00:13:53,958
-That's the plot of Home Alone.
-Gotcha.

266
00:13:54,041 --> 00:13:56,001
[chuckles] See,
I knew you weren't ignoring me.

267
00:13:57,002 --> 00:13:59,588
Did you bet that you could
make me popular or something?

268
00:14:00,464 --> 00:14:01,298
No, I--

269
00:14:01,382 --> 00:14:04,760
Because honestly, I have no desire
to act out that '90s rom-com.

270
00:14:06,387 --> 00:14:07,763
Ouch. [chuckles]

271
00:14:08,430 --> 00:14:10,391
Tell me how you really feel. [chuckles]

272
00:14:14,895 --> 00:14:16,730
Oh, I'm late for my shift.

273
00:14:21,068 --> 00:14:23,320
You really are all work and no play, huh?

274
00:14:24,738 --> 00:14:27,575
Yeah, well, not everyone
has the luxury to play.

275
00:14:37,710 --> 00:14:39,628
Hey, uh, so I was thinking, uh,

276
00:14:40,379 --> 00:14:42,047
these obstacle courses are cool and all,

277
00:14:42,131 --> 00:14:45,634
but maybe we can start scouting
broncs for me to take on?

278
00:14:45,718 --> 00:14:47,928
I mean, it's not like
I haven't done it before, right?

279
00:14:48,012 --> 00:14:49,638
Right, and how did that work out?

280
00:14:50,347 --> 00:14:53,434
You got bucked off and roughed up,
which brought you to me.

281
00:14:59,148 --> 00:15:00,024
Look, Alex,

282
00:15:00,524 --> 00:15:02,776
seriously, you've made some real progress,

283
00:15:02,860 --> 00:15:04,194
but you can't rush this.

284
00:15:04,278 --> 00:15:06,488
Every ride could be your last. Got it?

285
00:15:08,657 --> 00:15:09,658
Mm.

286
00:15:12,870 --> 00:15:14,622
Tomorrow, I figured
we'd take a field trip,

287
00:15:14,705 --> 00:15:16,582
scope out your competition.

288
00:15:16,665 --> 00:15:19,627
You know, unless you've got
something better to do.

289
00:15:19,710 --> 00:15:20,794
I'm all yours.

290
00:15:24,340 --> 00:15:26,342
[uplifting music playing]

291
00:15:29,637 --> 00:15:31,263
[Will] You're a lifesaver, Pat. Thank you.

292
00:15:31,347 --> 00:15:33,390
-[Pat] No problem. Talk to you later.
-Bye.

293
00:15:41,440 --> 00:15:43,651
Did you lose the keys
to your place or something?

294
00:15:43,734 --> 00:15:46,654
No. No, it just got
too quiet there without Hayley.

295
00:15:47,321 --> 00:15:48,447
You must miss her a lot.

296
00:15:48,530 --> 00:15:52,076
Yeah, but this semester abroad,
it's an incredible opportunity for her.

297
00:15:53,243 --> 00:15:56,038
She needs me to be supportive,
so I'm trying.

298
00:16:02,294 --> 00:16:05,047
Hey, Will, go easy on Dad, huh?

299
00:16:06,256 --> 00:16:07,299
He's trying too.

300
00:16:08,217 --> 00:16:10,219
[somber music playing]

301
00:16:17,351 --> 00:16:20,771
-You ready, champ?
-I've been ready for this my whole life.

302
00:16:28,320 --> 00:16:29,738
You want to talk about it?

303
00:16:35,035 --> 00:16:36,036
About?

304
00:16:38,455 --> 00:16:41,291
The reason you're home
on a Friday night watching Rudy.

305
00:16:41,792 --> 00:16:43,794
Hey, Rudy's a classic.

306
00:16:43,877 --> 00:16:47,381
Yeah, a classic that you only watch
after you've had a bad practice.

307
00:16:48,048 --> 00:16:51,927
Well, I'm more interested in talking about
whatever it is you've been up to.

308
00:16:53,053 --> 00:16:54,847
Where you been all gussied up?

309
00:16:55,764 --> 00:17:01,020
Oh, um, Amy had a few of us over
for some birthday cake and karaoke.

310
00:17:01,103 --> 00:17:01,937
Amy who?

311
00:17:03,564 --> 00:17:04,815
Amy from drama club.

312
00:17:07,359 --> 00:17:08,318
Sounds fun.

313
00:17:08,819 --> 00:17:09,737
For sure.

314
00:17:17,202 --> 00:17:18,954
[movie on TV resumes]

315
00:17:19,038 --> 00:17:21,040
[gentle music playing]

316
00:17:25,252 --> 00:17:27,254
[footsteps approaching]

317
00:17:29,465 --> 00:17:32,593
Hey, I was hoping we could go over
the schedule for driving lessons.

318
00:17:37,222 --> 00:17:38,057
Wow.

319
00:17:39,641 --> 00:17:41,268
I remember that collection.

320
00:17:42,978 --> 00:17:44,313
Vogue called it,

321
00:17:44,396 --> 00:17:47,441
"Effortlessly simple
contemporary glamour."

322
00:17:48,108 --> 00:17:51,028
[chuckles] Jewels by Angelica Howard.

323
00:17:52,696 --> 00:17:54,114
[Katherine] So, what's going on?

324
00:17:55,449 --> 00:17:57,910
Grace suggested that we take
a few to the pop-up.

325
00:17:59,745 --> 00:18:00,579
Oh.

326
00:18:03,082 --> 00:18:04,500
Well, what do you think?

327
00:18:06,335 --> 00:18:08,462
I made a list of pros and cons.

328
00:18:09,129 --> 00:18:11,715
And all of the reasons
why I should are valid.

329
00:18:12,257 --> 00:18:15,552
But I don't… I don't know.

330
00:18:16,220 --> 00:18:18,722
You know nobody would blame you
if you wanted to keep them.

331
00:18:18,806 --> 00:18:21,809
They're not just ordinary dresses.
They're your mom's art.

332
00:18:22,684 --> 00:18:26,313
Art that's meant to be worn,
not packed away in boxes.

333
00:18:32,277 --> 00:18:35,030
You know, way before your mom
started dressing all those celebrities,

334
00:18:35,114 --> 00:18:37,574
she would dress all of us
for all kinds of things.

335
00:18:39,034 --> 00:18:42,788
My junior year,
I was dating this guy, Brian something.

336
00:18:42,871 --> 00:18:45,541
And I remember one day he called me up

337
00:18:45,624 --> 00:18:47,918
and was like, "We need to talk."

338
00:18:48,544 --> 00:18:51,630
So… [scoffs]
…obviously I knew it was over.

339
00:18:51,713 --> 00:18:54,758
So what's your mom do?
She drags me out shopping,

340
00:18:54,842 --> 00:18:56,844
and she makes me buy this dress.

341
00:19:00,806 --> 00:19:02,933
I mean, talk about revenge dressing.

342
00:19:04,643 --> 00:19:07,229
She was all about making sure
that I felt bulletproof.

343
00:19:08,522 --> 00:19:11,942
"Fashion is the armor
to survive the reality of everyday life."

344
00:19:13,277 --> 00:19:15,696
It's a Bill Cunningham quote
she had on her desk.

345
00:19:16,989 --> 00:19:20,784
You know, Jackie, whatever decision
you make is the right one.

346
00:19:24,913 --> 00:19:28,250
And you're 100% sure
you don't want any of this stuff?

347
00:19:30,127 --> 00:19:30,961
Positive.

348
00:19:33,255 --> 00:19:36,175
Who knows? Maybe it'll be the armor
that somebody else needs.

349
00:19:38,677 --> 00:19:40,012
♪ When we were kids ♪

350
00:19:40,095 --> 00:19:44,057
♪ We were running around
With nothing else to do ♪

351
00:19:46,560 --> 00:19:48,145
♪ When we were kids… ♪

352
00:19:48,729 --> 00:19:50,063
So as we still need a feature

353
00:19:50,147 --> 00:19:52,858
for the "Here's What's Happening
in Silver Falls" section,

354
00:19:52,941 --> 00:19:55,444
I thought it's worth spotlighting
last week's town hall.

355
00:19:55,527 --> 00:19:56,778
People aren't exactly thrilled

356
00:19:56,862 --> 00:19:59,364
with the idea
of opening Silver Falls up to tourism.

357
00:20:00,324 --> 00:20:01,450
I don't know.

358
00:20:01,533 --> 00:20:02,451
[chuckles]

359
00:20:02,534 --> 00:20:04,161
Do you really think high schoolers care

360
00:20:04,244 --> 00:20:06,079
about what's happening
in my family's ranch?

361
00:20:06,163 --> 00:20:09,833
I mean, it's a significant development
that could affect the entire community.

362
00:20:13,462 --> 00:20:16,632
Okay, let's move on
to pop-up coverage, shall we?

363
00:20:17,341 --> 00:20:19,760
Zach's handling photography, obviously.

364
00:20:19,843 --> 00:20:20,761
Nate, it's your byline,

365
00:20:20,844 --> 00:20:22,554
but since you're pulling
double duty as DJ,

366
00:20:22,638 --> 00:20:24,932
which Student Council greatly appreciates,

367
00:20:25,015 --> 00:20:27,392
I'm happy to help gather
diverse perspectives,

368
00:20:27,476 --> 00:20:30,896
quotes, et cetera, on the core issue
behind the pop-up. Budget cuts.

369
00:20:30,979 --> 00:20:32,314
Yeah, okay.

370
00:20:32,397 --> 00:20:34,942
I'm also gonna talk to Mr. Duffy
about the marching band

371
00:20:35,025 --> 00:20:37,819
not getting the new uniforms
they were promised this year

372
00:20:37,903 --> 00:20:42,115
and Ms. Hampton about withdrawing from
the math Olympiad because of travel costs.

373
00:20:42,199 --> 00:20:45,702
But I mean, hey, as long as school sports
is thriving, it's all good, right?

374
00:20:45,786 --> 00:20:47,246
[Skylar] Exactly.

375
00:20:47,329 --> 00:20:50,040
This isn't the time for a puff piece.
Don't hold back.

376
00:20:52,709 --> 00:20:54,211
♪ Don't hold back ♪

377
00:20:54,878 --> 00:20:58,674
♪ I want to break free
'Cause it's singing through your body ♪

378
00:20:59,341 --> 00:21:01,927
♪ And I'm carried by the sound ♪

379
00:21:02,010 --> 00:21:03,679
Of course you know Perfume Genius.

380
00:21:04,972 --> 00:21:08,558
I mean, it's not exactly
as obscure as Trash Dolls, so…

381
00:21:09,184 --> 00:21:10,602
And are these bands?

382
00:21:14,147 --> 00:21:16,900
-Well…
-Perfume Genius is one guy.

383
00:21:16,984 --> 00:21:18,402
But Trash Dolls is a band.

384
00:21:19,069 --> 00:21:22,197
As you can see, Zach,
I'd be lost musically without this one.

385
00:21:22,948 --> 00:21:24,116
You're welcome.

386
00:21:24,199 --> 00:21:25,075
[chuckles]

387
00:21:25,784 --> 00:21:26,702
Mm.

388
00:21:27,286 --> 00:21:29,329
I think I need a refill. Anyone else?

389
00:21:29,413 --> 00:21:30,706
-Nope.
-No, thanks.

390
00:21:33,792 --> 00:21:34,835
[Nathan] Hmm.

391
00:21:35,544 --> 00:21:38,213
[scoffs] I think someone's got
a little crush on you.

392
00:21:39,381 --> 00:21:40,590
No. [chuckles]

393
00:21:40,674 --> 00:21:43,969
We… we like similar music and…

394
00:21:44,803 --> 00:21:49,016
Hey, even if he… even if he did,
I'm happily taken.

395
00:21:50,475 --> 00:21:51,935
Damn right you are.

396
00:21:52,019 --> 00:21:53,687
-[Nathan] Mm-hmm.
-[Skylar chuckles]

397
00:21:56,315 --> 00:21:58,317
[footsteps approaching]

398
00:22:00,861 --> 00:22:01,862
[Jackie] Alex!

399
00:22:01,945 --> 00:22:04,489
I could've seriously hurt you.

400
00:22:04,573 --> 00:22:06,575
You know,
you're getting pretty good at that.

401
00:22:07,367 --> 00:22:10,078
If I didn't know any better,
I'd say you grew up on a ranch.

402
00:22:11,621 --> 00:22:12,622
Okay, well,

403
00:22:13,498 --> 00:22:14,624
have a nice ride.

404
00:22:15,625 --> 00:22:16,835
Thanks.

405
00:22:18,420 --> 00:22:19,379
Will do.

406
00:22:24,092 --> 00:22:25,427
Have a nice ride?

407
00:22:31,683 --> 00:22:32,768
[door closes]

408
00:22:36,772 --> 00:22:38,023
What happened to you?

409
00:22:39,358 --> 00:22:40,275
Chores.

410
00:22:42,361 --> 00:22:43,653
Want some coffee?

411
00:22:43,737 --> 00:22:46,239
More like need, desperately.

412
00:22:49,242 --> 00:22:53,246
Hey, um, have you noticed
anything weird about Danny lately?

413
00:22:53,330 --> 00:22:54,581
Uh…

414
00:22:55,457 --> 00:22:56,291
Weird how?

415
00:22:56,917 --> 00:23:01,880
I don't know, like,
did anything happen over the summer?

416
00:23:01,963 --> 00:23:04,341
If you're worried something's up,
why not just ask him?

417
00:23:04,966 --> 00:23:08,845
I don't know. I'm probably
just imagining it or something.

418
00:23:11,848 --> 00:23:13,850
[mysterious music playing]

419
00:23:21,525 --> 00:23:22,651
Easy, there's…

420
00:23:23,693 --> 00:23:25,654
It's just there's hay in your hair.

421
00:23:25,737 --> 00:23:27,739
[upbeat music playing]

422
00:23:30,659 --> 00:23:31,701
Got it.

423
00:23:33,412 --> 00:23:34,538
[door opens]

424
00:23:36,540 --> 00:23:38,083
-[George] Oh, hey, Jackie.
-Hi.

425
00:23:38,917 --> 00:23:40,293
Hey, how you doing?

426
00:23:40,377 --> 00:23:41,211
Great.

427
00:23:42,546 --> 00:23:45,298
Yeah, I hear practice was tricky, huh?

428
00:23:45,882 --> 00:23:47,843
That's one way to put it, yeah.

429
00:23:47,926 --> 00:23:49,761
[George] You want to tell me about it?

430
00:23:51,346 --> 00:23:54,349
I thought… I thought Dylan was
gonna make this easier for me.

431
00:23:55,976 --> 00:23:57,727
But he's undermining me
every chance he gets.

432
00:23:58,395 --> 00:23:59,229
Hmm.

433
00:23:59,312 --> 00:24:01,565
Unless I'm just a lousy coach.

434
00:24:01,648 --> 00:24:03,692
Well, you're not a lousy coach. All right?

435
00:24:03,775 --> 00:24:07,487
Allen offered you this job because
you're a natural-born leader, right?

436
00:24:07,571 --> 00:24:08,822
Nobody knows the game like you.

437
00:24:09,406 --> 00:24:10,282
You're in a new role.

438
00:24:10,365 --> 00:24:12,242
It's gonna take a minute
to get their respect.

439
00:24:12,325 --> 00:24:14,536
It's kinda hard to get respect
and be a leader

440
00:24:14,619 --> 00:24:17,289
when your starting quarterback
refuses to listen to you.

441
00:24:18,457 --> 00:24:21,918
-I don't want to fail at this.
-Well, you keep being you.

442
00:24:22,461 --> 00:24:24,754
All right? Trust your instincts.
It'll get through.

443
00:24:33,180 --> 00:24:35,557
Okay, team. How are we looking?

444
00:24:35,640 --> 00:24:37,309
To put it lightly, bleak.

445
00:24:37,809 --> 00:24:39,895
Super helpful, Olivia. Thank you.

446
00:24:39,978 --> 00:24:41,771
I'm just pointing out the obvious.

447
00:24:41,855 --> 00:24:45,650
We promised people vintage.
It's all giving burn-after-wearing.

448
00:24:46,234 --> 00:24:48,069
I've got two more boxes in my car.

449
00:24:48,153 --> 00:24:51,531
Let me guess. More treasures
from the church lost and found?

450
00:24:51,615 --> 00:24:55,452
Funny, but no. Actually, Jackie sent me
over with some old stuff of Katherine's.

451
00:24:55,535 --> 00:24:57,787
Hold on, where is Jackie?

452
00:24:57,871 --> 00:25:00,624
Hi. I brought reinforcements.

453
00:25:01,917 --> 00:25:03,543
Now this is more like it!

454
00:25:04,044 --> 00:25:06,379
No way those belong to Cole's mom.

455
00:25:06,963 --> 00:25:09,216
Actually, my mom designed these.

456
00:25:18,225 --> 00:25:21,269
Jackie, I can't believe you brought them.

457
00:25:28,401 --> 00:25:29,694
[door opens]

458
00:25:38,870 --> 00:25:40,372
-Hi, babe.
-Hmm.

459
00:25:41,122 --> 00:25:43,041
That bulldozer hasn't moved
since yesterday,

460
00:25:43,124 --> 00:25:45,293
so I think you can end your watch.

461
00:25:46,253 --> 00:25:48,296
Or they're just waiting for me
to let my guard down.

462
00:25:48,380 --> 00:25:49,714
[Katherine chuckles]

463
00:25:50,715 --> 00:25:51,716
Oh.

464
00:25:52,217 --> 00:25:53,176
Where are you off to?

465
00:25:53,260 --> 00:25:56,555
I gotta go to the clinic, and then
I'm gonna meet Lori for a drink later.

466
00:25:56,638 --> 00:25:59,057
-Nice.
-And I think I might stop by the pop-up.

467
00:25:59,140 --> 00:26:01,726
And just make sure Jackie's okay.

468
00:26:01,810 --> 00:26:03,311
Well, why wouldn't she be okay?

469
00:26:03,937 --> 00:26:06,982
Apparently, she decided to take
Angelica's dresses after all.

470
00:26:07,065 --> 00:26:09,442
Oh, well, I mean, that's progress, right?

471
00:26:09,526 --> 00:26:10,527
[Katherine] Maybe.

472
00:26:10,610 --> 00:26:11,570
[footsteps approaching]

473
00:26:11,653 --> 00:26:13,738
-Or maybe not. I don't know.
-Well, we'll see.

474
00:26:14,781 --> 00:26:16,283
-Hey, Mom.
-Hi, honey.

475
00:26:17,075 --> 00:26:18,076
How are you?

476
00:26:18,159 --> 00:26:19,411
Good. Dad?

477
00:26:19,494 --> 00:26:20,579
William.

478
00:26:20,662 --> 00:26:22,455
I was thinking we could go fly-fishing.

479
00:26:22,539 --> 00:26:23,999
-[George] Hmm.
-[Will] Today.

480
00:26:25,166 --> 00:26:27,836
Uh… no. No, no,
I got some hay bales coming,

481
00:26:27,919 --> 00:26:29,379
and I gotta place a grain order, so…

482
00:26:29,462 --> 00:26:32,549
And we figured you'd say that,
so Lee's gonna take care of the hay bales,

483
00:26:32,632 --> 00:26:34,467
and Danny's on top of the grain order.

484
00:26:36,386 --> 00:26:37,387
[George sighs]

485
00:26:38,013 --> 00:26:39,139
You need a day off.

486
00:26:40,265 --> 00:26:41,266
You both do.

487
00:26:44,394 --> 00:26:45,812
-Please.
-[George sighs]

488
00:26:47,355 --> 00:26:49,316
Well, why not? Sure.

489
00:26:49,399 --> 00:26:50,358
[Katherine] Good.

490
00:26:52,152 --> 00:26:53,695
The ranch isn't going anywhere.

491
00:26:57,324 --> 00:26:59,326
["In Between Days" playing]

492
00:27:06,791 --> 00:27:09,711
♪ Yesterday I got so old ♪

493
00:27:09,794 --> 00:27:12,631
♪ I felt like I could die ♪

494
00:27:13,506 --> 00:27:16,509
♪ Yesterday I got so old ♪

495
00:27:16,593 --> 00:27:19,220
♪ It made me want to cry ♪

496
00:27:19,721 --> 00:27:23,224
♪ Go on, go on, just walk away ♪

497
00:27:23,308 --> 00:27:26,478
♪ Go on, go on, your choice is made ♪

498
00:27:26,561 --> 00:27:29,939
♪ Go on, go on, and disappear ♪

499
00:27:30,023 --> 00:27:33,109
♪ Go on, go on, away from here ♪

500
00:27:33,193 --> 00:27:36,571
♪ And I know I was wrong
When I said it was true ♪

501
00:27:36,655 --> 00:27:38,198
♪ That it couldn't be me ♪

502
00:27:38,281 --> 00:27:39,908
♪ And be her in between ♪

503
00:27:39,991 --> 00:27:41,868
♪ Without you ♪

504
00:27:43,286 --> 00:27:45,497
♪ Without you… ♪

505
00:27:46,873 --> 00:27:48,083
[Grace] Kiley!

506
00:27:48,166 --> 00:27:50,293
You should get one. For the dance.

507
00:27:50,377 --> 00:27:53,880
School dances are against my religion…
and my work schedule.

508
00:27:53,963 --> 00:27:56,675
-♪ Yesterday I got so scared… ♪
-[phone ringing]

509
00:27:56,758 --> 00:27:57,676
Duty calls.

510
00:27:59,552 --> 00:28:00,553
[overlapping chatter]

511
00:28:00,637 --> 00:28:03,723
♪ Yesterday away from you ♪

512
00:28:03,807 --> 00:28:05,475
♪ It froze me deep inside… ♪

513
00:28:05,558 --> 00:28:07,185
Okay, here you go.

514
00:28:07,268 --> 00:28:10,313
♪ Come back, come back
Don't walk away… ♪

515
00:28:10,397 --> 00:28:11,731
Is everything okay over here?

516
00:28:12,607 --> 00:28:15,652
Yeah. Thank you
for supporting SFH Student Council.

517
00:28:16,903 --> 00:28:20,490
♪ Come back, come back, come back to me… ♪

518
00:28:21,366 --> 00:28:22,492
Jackie,

519
00:28:23,159 --> 00:28:25,704
I know you don't want
or need my two cents,

520
00:28:25,787 --> 00:28:28,289
but I'm giving it anyway, okay?

521
00:28:30,792 --> 00:28:33,002
I think donating those dresses
was really brave.

522
00:28:34,129 --> 00:28:36,047
Why? They're just things.

523
00:28:37,340 --> 00:28:40,510
♪ Without you ♪

524
00:28:40,593 --> 00:28:42,887
♪ Without you ♪

525
00:28:54,607 --> 00:28:57,026
Hey, you need a hand?

526
00:28:57,110 --> 00:28:57,986
I've got it.

527
00:29:08,955 --> 00:29:10,665
What are we doing here, Will?

528
00:29:11,875 --> 00:29:13,334
'Cause you hate fly-fishing.

529
00:29:15,295 --> 00:29:17,881
Are you really on board
with this guest ranch idea?

530
00:29:20,216 --> 00:29:23,011
'Cause lately it's like
we're not on the same page, Dad.

531
00:29:24,304 --> 00:29:27,182
First with the town hall,
then with the shed. I mean…

532
00:29:27,682 --> 00:29:29,434
I'm on board, I promise you.

533
00:29:30,351 --> 00:29:31,186
It's just…

534
00:29:32,437 --> 00:29:35,940
I don't want to wake up one morning
and not even recognize my own backyard.

535
00:29:36,441 --> 00:29:38,109
And you think I want that?

536
00:29:38,610 --> 00:29:40,278
It's not you that I'm worried about.

537
00:29:41,362 --> 00:29:44,115
Look, I like Richard well enough.
Like, he's Jackie's uncle,

538
00:29:44,199 --> 00:29:47,118
but doesn't mean
I trust him with our ranch.

539
00:29:47,786 --> 00:29:48,912
Then trust me.

540
00:29:50,163 --> 00:29:50,997
I do.

541
00:29:54,584 --> 00:29:56,836
I'm sorry if I've acted like I didn't.

542
00:30:01,090 --> 00:30:02,133
Thanks for saying that.

543
00:30:06,221 --> 00:30:07,138
Okay.

544
00:30:08,389 --> 00:30:10,683
Show me what I'm doing wrong, please.

545
00:30:11,184 --> 00:30:12,519
Well, for starters…

546
00:30:14,354 --> 00:30:17,148
everything, Will. [laughs]

547
00:30:17,232 --> 00:30:20,401
Okay, hey, look.
Okay, pinch the line. Start with that.

548
00:30:20,485 --> 00:30:22,403
-Okay. All right.
-You gotta control the line.

549
00:30:22,487 --> 00:30:24,489
["Connection" playing]

550
00:30:29,244 --> 00:30:30,411
I know what you're doing.

551
00:30:32,330 --> 00:30:34,207
Shooting the pop-up for the paper?

552
00:30:34,290 --> 00:30:35,792
That's not all you're doing.

553
00:30:35,875 --> 00:30:37,919
I'm just documenting
like any good journalist would.

554
00:30:38,002 --> 00:30:40,171
♪ Riding on any wave ♪

555
00:30:40,255 --> 00:30:42,173
♪ That is the luck you crave ♪

556
00:30:42,257 --> 00:30:44,092
♪ They don't believe it now ♪

557
00:30:44,175 --> 00:30:45,802
♪ They just think it's stupid ♪

558
00:30:45,885 --> 00:30:48,054
♪So, got anything? ♪

559
00:30:48,137 --> 00:30:49,889
♪ Anyone could've done ♪

560
00:30:49,973 --> 00:30:51,558
♪ Who woul'dve cared at all? ♪

561
00:30:51,641 --> 00:30:53,017
♪ Not you ♪

562
00:30:54,394 --> 00:30:55,854
♪ Another heart ♪

563
00:30:56,813 --> 00:30:58,231
♪ Has made the trade ♪

564
00:30:58,857 --> 00:30:59,732
♪ Forget it ♪

565
00:30:59,816 --> 00:31:01,442
♪ Forget it, forget it ♪

566
00:31:01,526 --> 00:31:04,654
♪ I don't understand
How a heart is a spade… ♪

567
00:31:04,737 --> 00:31:05,822
[Ruby] Cole!

568
00:31:05,905 --> 00:31:08,366
♪ But somehow
A vital connection is made… ♪

569
00:31:08,449 --> 00:31:09,534
What do you think?

570
00:31:10,618 --> 00:31:11,661
[sighs]

571
00:31:11,744 --> 00:31:12,620
Very nice.

572
00:31:14,330 --> 00:31:15,540
Where were you last night?

573
00:31:17,250 --> 00:31:20,670
-What was last night?
-Dylan invited the whole team over?

574
00:31:22,088 --> 00:31:22,964
Oh.

575
00:31:23,965 --> 00:31:26,509
If it makes you feel any better,
you didn't miss anything.

576
00:31:27,302 --> 00:31:28,303
I'm sure.

577
00:31:30,013 --> 00:31:32,223
Hey! Isn't this the coolest?

578
00:31:32,724 --> 00:31:35,602
Skylar just spoke to Mato,
and he's super happy with everything.

579
00:31:35,685 --> 00:31:37,604
We might actually pull this off.

580
00:31:41,441 --> 00:31:42,275
Oh no.

581
00:31:44,861 --> 00:31:45,695
Um…

582
00:31:46,195 --> 00:31:48,531
Hey! What the hell is wrong with you?

583
00:31:48,615 --> 00:31:52,160
-Relax.
-Do not tell me to relax, Ruby.

584
00:31:52,243 --> 00:31:55,246
Hey, Jackie, it's not that big a deal.

585
00:31:55,330 --> 00:31:58,875
If the dress were supposed to have a slit,
it would have come with one.

586
00:31:58,958 --> 00:32:02,545
Maybe if you cared about them so much,
you should've left them at home.

587
00:32:02,629 --> 00:32:03,755
Okay, maybe let's not do this

588
00:32:03,838 --> 00:32:06,549
in front of the people we're counting on
to fund our dance.

589
00:32:06,633 --> 00:32:08,051
Ruby, go take that off!

590
00:32:08,134 --> 00:32:10,011
You broke it, you buy it.

591
00:32:10,094 --> 00:32:11,429
Nathan, music.

592
00:32:13,306 --> 00:32:14,766
-Jackie…
-I'm taking a walk.

593
00:32:16,559 --> 00:32:18,561
Cole, let her go.

594
00:32:19,103 --> 00:32:20,271
She needs a minute.

595
00:32:26,694 --> 00:32:27,528
[sighs]

596
00:32:27,612 --> 00:32:28,446
[Katherine] Jackie?

597
00:32:30,281 --> 00:32:31,115
Jackie.

598
00:32:32,867 --> 00:32:34,035
Is everything okay?

599
00:32:37,121 --> 00:32:38,915
Just needed some fresh air.

600
00:32:38,998 --> 00:32:39,958
[Katherine] Hmm.

601
00:32:40,750 --> 00:32:42,460
Got a little, uh, stuffy in there?

602
00:32:43,086 --> 00:32:44,337
Yeah. [chuckles]

603
00:32:50,969 --> 00:32:53,513
One of the girls tore
one of my mom's dresses.

604
00:32:53,596 --> 00:32:55,223
She tore an Angelica Howard original?

605
00:32:55,306 --> 00:32:56,557
She wanted a slit.

606
00:32:56,641 --> 00:32:57,642
[Katherine scoffs]

607
00:32:59,310 --> 00:33:00,144
Okay.

608
00:33:01,437 --> 00:33:02,438
What's her name?

609
00:33:02,939 --> 00:33:05,316
'Cause I'm gonna go in there,
rip that dress out of her hands,

610
00:33:05,400 --> 00:33:07,026
and I'm gonna take it home and fix it.

611
00:33:08,611 --> 00:33:09,862
It's okay. [chuckles]

612
00:33:11,280 --> 00:33:15,410
I guess I just wasn't expecting it
to be so hard to let them go.

613
00:33:20,581 --> 00:33:21,833
Do you want to go home?

614
00:33:23,042 --> 00:33:25,378
I'll be fine. I just… I need a minute.

615
00:33:28,673 --> 00:33:29,590
And a hug?

616
00:33:32,010 --> 00:33:32,844
Yeah.

617
00:33:33,344 --> 00:33:35,179
[emotional music playing]

618
00:33:38,558 --> 00:33:39,642
[horn blows]

619
00:33:39,726 --> 00:33:41,728
[upbeat country music playing]

620
00:33:54,657 --> 00:33:56,576
Okay, that's Wylder Holt.

621
00:33:56,659 --> 00:33:59,454
He's a rising star
among bronc riders under 25

622
00:33:59,537 --> 00:34:00,913
and the reason why we're here.

623
00:34:02,123 --> 00:34:03,207
So pay attention.

624
00:34:11,299 --> 00:34:13,551
-[Wylder] Okay!
-[energetic music playing]

625
00:34:25,188 --> 00:34:26,731
[horn blows]

626
00:34:29,317 --> 00:34:30,443
I give it 80 out of 100.

627
00:34:30,526 --> 00:34:32,403
Oh, tough critic.

628
00:34:43,039 --> 00:34:43,915
[music ends]

629
00:34:47,960 --> 00:34:48,961
Hi, Wylder.

630
00:34:50,129 --> 00:34:51,839
-It's been a minute.
-Blake Hartford.

631
00:34:51,923 --> 00:34:54,092
It has indeed. Who's your friend?

632
00:34:54,175 --> 00:34:56,219
Wylder Holt, Alex Walter.

633
00:34:56,302 --> 00:34:58,346
Alex here is chasing the adrenaline rush.

634
00:34:58,429 --> 00:35:01,516
Well, if anyone can whip you
into bucking shape, Blake's your gal.

635
00:35:01,599 --> 00:35:02,892
Bronc riding's in her blood.

636
00:35:02,975 --> 00:35:06,145
Yeah. My daddy still
would've preferred a son, though.

637
00:35:06,229 --> 00:35:09,482
Hartford, you have more cojones
than half the guys on our circuit.

638
00:35:10,525 --> 00:35:11,901
I wish I could stay and hang,

639
00:35:11,984 --> 00:35:13,903
but we're due in Vegas tomorrow
bright and early.

640
00:35:14,654 --> 00:35:15,947
Don't be a stranger, yeah?

641
00:35:16,906 --> 00:35:19,325
Hope to meet you
in the arena one day, Alex Walter.

642
00:35:23,371 --> 00:35:25,623
See? I know my shit.

643
00:35:25,706 --> 00:35:28,042
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-[Blake chuckles]

644
00:35:28,126 --> 00:35:33,464
Just like I know there's one thing
holding Wylder back from true greatness.

645
00:35:34,048 --> 00:35:35,216
Any guesses, class?

646
00:35:35,967 --> 00:35:39,053
-He fights the ride instead of joining it.
-Bingo.

647
00:35:39,137 --> 00:35:41,931
Just hanging on
doesn't make a real cowboy.

648
00:35:42,014 --> 00:35:45,726
It's about connecting,
like you do with Murphy.

649
00:35:46,310 --> 00:35:49,730
Do this right, and soon enough
Wylder will be chasing your dust,

650
00:35:50,356 --> 00:35:51,274
not vice versa.

651
00:35:53,151 --> 00:35:55,528
But we should probably
be getting you home.

652
00:35:56,362 --> 00:35:59,323
Or maybe we don't
have to call it a night just yet.

653
00:36:01,075 --> 00:36:02,535
Aren't you training early?

654
00:36:02,618 --> 00:36:05,746
Word on the street,
your coach is a hard-ass.

655
00:36:05,830 --> 00:36:07,915
Nothing I can't handle.

656
00:36:09,667 --> 00:36:10,501
Okay.

657
00:36:11,752 --> 00:36:12,712
Lead the way.

658
00:36:16,048 --> 00:36:17,258
Alex Walter.

659
00:36:17,925 --> 00:36:19,010
[chuckles]

660
00:36:21,512 --> 00:36:23,514
[country music playing on radio]

661
00:36:25,725 --> 00:36:29,270
♪ Turn the radio up
Sing along to the song-- ♪

662
00:36:35,443 --> 00:36:36,277
Hey, Will.

663
00:36:36,777 --> 00:36:38,905
Let's, um… let's do this again, huh?

664
00:36:38,988 --> 00:36:39,989
Yeah, that'd be great.

665
00:36:40,072 --> 00:36:42,033
Next time it doesn't
have to be something you hate.

666
00:36:42,116 --> 00:36:43,075
[scoffs]

667
00:36:43,159 --> 00:36:44,827
[horse whinnies]

668
00:36:45,828 --> 00:36:50,499
I couldn't remember the exact location
of the old silo, so hopefully this works.

669
00:36:56,380 --> 00:36:57,423
Dad,

670
00:36:58,007 --> 00:37:01,594
the ranch, its history,
they're important to me too.

671
00:37:03,012 --> 00:37:05,181
I want this to work because I care.

672
00:37:06,182 --> 00:37:08,142
Sometimes about the wrong things, but

673
00:37:09,435 --> 00:37:10,561
I'll do better.

674
00:37:12,396 --> 00:37:13,356
We both will.

675
00:37:20,071 --> 00:37:21,197
♪ I pace ♪

676
00:37:21,280 --> 00:37:22,823
♪ I run my mouth ♪

677
00:37:22,907 --> 00:37:25,243
♪ I pray and wait ♪

678
00:37:25,326 --> 00:37:28,287
♪ I cross out his name on the page ♪

679
00:37:28,913 --> 00:37:32,333
♪ How long till this washes away? ♪

680
00:37:32,959 --> 00:37:34,335
♪ How long till ♪

681
00:37:34,418 --> 00:37:37,004
♪ My body is safe? ♪

682
00:37:37,088 --> 00:37:38,381
♪ How long till ♪

683
00:37:38,464 --> 00:37:40,424
♪ I walk in the light? ♪

684
00:37:40,925 --> 00:37:42,426
♪ How long till ♪

685
00:37:42,510 --> 00:37:44,428
♪ This heart isn't mine? ♪

686
00:37:44,512 --> 00:37:48,057
♪ The rise and fall of his chest on me ♪

687
00:37:52,603 --> 00:37:56,524
♪ I'm trying, but still it's all I see… ♪

688
00:38:01,487 --> 00:38:04,323
-Oh. Hi.
-Oh, hi.

689
00:38:04,407 --> 00:38:05,825
I didn't hear you come in.

690
00:38:05,908 --> 00:38:08,452
Yeah, I ran in here
to get a head start on my article.

691
00:38:08,536 --> 00:38:09,370
Great.

692
00:38:10,705 --> 00:38:13,416
-So, how'd the pop-up go?
-You know, I'd say it was a success.

693
00:38:13,499 --> 00:38:16,585
When I left, most of the racks were empty.
Jackie's dresses were gone.

694
00:38:17,169 --> 00:38:18,004
Oh.

695
00:38:18,087 --> 00:38:22,049
♪ I promise every day to change… ♪

696
00:38:22,133 --> 00:38:23,175
[Katherine] Nice photo.

697
00:38:24,010 --> 00:38:25,886
Looks like you caught someone's eye.

698
00:38:27,471 --> 00:38:28,306
Cutie.

699
00:38:29,890 --> 00:38:31,183
♪ How long till ♪

700
00:38:31,267 --> 00:38:33,936
♪ My body is safe? ♪

701
00:38:34,020 --> 00:38:35,354
♪ How long till ♪

702
00:38:35,438 --> 00:38:37,440
♪ I walk in the light? ♪

703
00:38:38,149 --> 00:38:40,985
We could offer a journey through time
on horseback, you know,

704
00:38:41,068 --> 00:38:43,654
showcasing the barn,
the shed, the cider cart,

705
00:38:43,738 --> 00:38:45,614
that creek where Amos Walter struck gold.

706
00:38:45,698 --> 00:38:49,201
Let's make our family history
a living part of the business, you know?

707
00:38:49,285 --> 00:38:50,870
Will, I love that idea. It's great.

708
00:38:50,953 --> 00:38:53,414
But Amos Walter struck pyrite.

709
00:38:53,497 --> 00:38:54,373
[Will chuckles]

710
00:38:54,457 --> 00:38:57,460
Yeah, but, "Come see
where Amos Walter found fool's gold"

711
00:38:57,543 --> 00:38:58,794
doesn't have the same ring.

712
00:38:58,878 --> 00:38:59,879
Oh, good!

713
00:38:59,962 --> 00:39:02,131
-[George] Oh, hey!
-I can call off the search party.

714
00:39:02,214 --> 00:39:04,258
[chuckles] Sorry.
We stopped to get a bite to eat.

715
00:39:04,342 --> 00:39:05,301
Mission accomplished.

716
00:39:06,218 --> 00:39:07,970
-[door opens]
-[Richard] Anyone home?

717
00:39:08,471 --> 00:39:09,305
[door closes]

718
00:39:11,766 --> 00:39:14,435
Richard. Hey, what are you doing here?

719
00:39:14,518 --> 00:39:15,603
Is this about Jackie?

720
00:39:16,270 --> 00:39:17,229
Uh…

721
00:39:17,897 --> 00:39:19,065
Not exactly.

722
00:39:21,859 --> 00:39:24,403
-Look, there's no easy way to say this.
-[George] So just say it.

723
00:39:28,407 --> 00:39:29,283
Okay.

724
00:39:29,909 --> 00:39:32,995
I'm here 'cause you bungled the town hall,
and we can't allow this community

725
00:39:33,079 --> 00:39:34,705
to delay breaking ground any further.

726
00:39:35,289 --> 00:39:37,416
We don't have the time
or the money to play games.

727
00:39:38,417 --> 00:39:40,086
How'd you hear about town hall?

728
00:39:40,586 --> 00:39:42,171
Keeping tabs on us?

729
00:39:46,759 --> 00:39:47,968
Because I called him.

730
00:39:48,469 --> 00:39:50,471
[tense music playing]

731
00:40:02,149 --> 00:40:04,235
So, what's the verdict?

732
00:40:04,985 --> 00:40:07,738
Well, with our cut of the pizza sales,
plus clothes,

733
00:40:07,822 --> 00:40:10,032
we made over $200 more than our goal.

734
00:40:10,116 --> 00:40:11,158
Okay.

735
00:40:12,368 --> 00:40:16,330
I have to admit,
you do have some good ideas. Sometimes.

736
00:40:16,914 --> 00:40:18,791
I am gonna need that in writing.

737
00:40:20,918 --> 00:40:25,089
Um, about earlier, I know
I shouldn't have blown up like that.

738
00:40:25,798 --> 00:40:26,841
Don't apologize.

739
00:40:28,050 --> 00:40:31,637
I meant what I said.
Donating those dresses was really brave.

740
00:40:33,556 --> 00:40:35,724
That kind of bravery
deserves to be rewarded.

741
00:40:44,358 --> 00:40:45,359
I thought…

742
00:40:47,486 --> 00:40:50,698
Erin, you set this aside for me?

743
00:40:53,826 --> 00:40:56,203
I know that if I found
something of my dad's,

744
00:40:56,287 --> 00:40:59,206
I… never want to let it go.

745
00:41:01,417 --> 00:41:03,419
Besides, it's totally you.

746
00:41:04,295 --> 00:41:07,715
Now you have the perfect dress
to wear to the dance that you saved.

747
00:41:13,095 --> 00:41:14,096
[Alex sighs]

748
00:41:15,431 --> 00:41:16,390
[sighs]

749
00:41:17,391 --> 00:41:18,392
Hey, Kiley.

750
00:41:18,476 --> 00:41:19,768
I'll give you a few minutes.

751
00:41:25,524 --> 00:41:27,776
I'm headed out,
if you want to roll with me.

752
00:41:29,862 --> 00:41:32,364
Friends give friends rides home sometimes.

753
00:41:33,282 --> 00:41:35,826
But you can ride in the back seat.

754
00:41:35,910 --> 00:41:38,370
Pretend to be a chauffeur
if it makes you feel more comfortable.

755
00:41:42,958 --> 00:41:45,169
[pensive music playing]

756
00:41:45,252 --> 00:41:46,295
[Alex] All right.

757
00:41:47,338 --> 00:41:48,839
